--- !u!114 &1000032
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1000030}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6b3d9f1c5a7e40289d4b6f8a2c0e1537, type: 3}
  m_Name:
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  _Title: 04 - Your ForceApplier
  _Objective: Put YOUR ForceApplier on each cube, set it up the way the cube is named,
    and press play. One component, four setups, four different behaviours.
  _NewThisLevel: 'Nothing is set up for you - the cubes are bare Rigidbodies; Same
    mass and same gravity everywhere, so the only thing that changes is HOW you push;
    1 and 2 push through the centre, 3 and 4 push at a point; AddForceAtPosition
    wants a WORLD point - transform.TransformPoint turns your local one into it;
    The corner of these cubes is local (0.5, 0.5, 0), not (1, 1, 0); Only 3 and 4
    are allowed to rotate, so a tumble there is real'
  _PanelWidth: 320
  _ScreenMargin: 12
  _ShowOnStart: 1
  _ToggleKey: 22
